1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
For millions of senior citizens navigating digital India, a single deceptive link can lead to devastating loss.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Fear tactics, fake banking portals, and confusing payment traps prey on urgency and low digital literacy.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Meet Sakha — a calm, on-device digital safety companion designed specifically for elders.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,500
Sakha runs completely inside the browser as a Manifest V3 extension, protecting pages without sending personal data away.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Watch what happens when an elder lands on a counterfeit verification page.

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:41,500
In just 0.068 milliseconds on our hold-out benchmark (RESULTS.md §1), Sakha detects the lookalike domain and credential combo.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,500
Instead of panic, Sakha presents a calm, high-contrast, bilingual warning in English and Telugu.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,500
It explains plainly what is wrong, and provides one large, accessible button to leave safely.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,500
In benchmark testing across 60 scenarios, Sakha achieved a 100% scam detection rate with 0% false alarms (RESULTS.md §1).

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Next, on genuine forms, Sakha safeguards privacy through automatic on-page blurring.

11
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:17,500
In just 13 milliseconds on heavy DOM trees (RESULTS.md §2), Aadhaar, PAN, and cards are masked from shoulder-surfers.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,500
When needed, the senior can tap once to peek, verify their details, and tap to hide them again.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
When an elder needs help understanding an unfamiliar form, they can open Sakha in Telugu or Hindi.

14
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:38,500
The Explain helper summarizes the page in two simple sentences, using only masked text with zero PII.

15
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,500
Most importantly, look at the network panel. Exactly zero bytes leave the machine (RESULTS.md §3).

16
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,500
No Aadhaar digits, passwords, or browsing history are ever transmitted off-device.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Sakha is built for accessible dignity: large touch targets, WCAG double-A contrast, and on-device privacy.

18
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:10,000
Empowering India's seniors to browse with confidence. Open source at github.com/sathvikbadam/Sakha.
